  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 14,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.104,
            0.194,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "TRIANGLES"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.873,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "87"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.138,
            0.902,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let rays BP and CQ intersect each other at A and rays ER and FS intersect each other at D. In the two triangles ABC and DEF, you can see that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{E}, \\angle \\mathrm{C} = \\angle \\mathrm{F}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{D}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . That is, corresponding angles of these two triangles are equal. What can you say about their corresponding sides ? Note that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { B C } } { \\mathrm { E F } }   =   \\frac { 3 } { 5 }   =   0 . 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . What about "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { A B } } { \\mathrm { D E } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { C A } } { \\mathrm { F D } }   _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " On measuring AB, DE, CA and FD, you will find that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { A B } } { \\mathrm { D E } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { C A } } { \\mathrm { F D } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are also equal to 0.6 (or nearly equal to 0.6, if there is some error in the measurement). Thus, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { A B } } { \\mathrm { D E } } = \\frac { \\mathrm { B C } } { \\mathrm { E F } } = \\frac { \\mathrm { C A } } { \\mathrm { F D } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " You can repeat this activity by constructing several pairs of triangles having their corresponding angles equal. Every time, you will find that their corresponding sides are in the same ratio (or proportion). This activity leads us to the following criterion for similarity of two triangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.389,
            0.902,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Theorem 6.3 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If in two triangles, corresponding angles are equal, then their corresponding sides are in the same ratio (or proportion) and hence the two triangles are similar. D"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.454,
            0.489,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This criterion is referred to as the AAA (Angle–Angle–Angle) criterion of similarity of two triangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.517,
            0.488,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This theorem can be proved by taking two triangles ABC and DEF such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{D}, \\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{E}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{C} = \\angle \\mathrm{F}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (see Fig. 6.24)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.499,
            0.435,
            0.899,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.499,
                0.435,
                0.899,
                0.573
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.655,
                0.584,
                0.755,
                0.603
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.24"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.599,
            0.498,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cut "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { D P } = \\mathrm { A B }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{DQ} = \\mathrm{AC}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and join PQ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.626,
            0.135,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.38,
            0.625,
            0.718,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ΔABC ≡ Δ DPQ (Why ?)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.652,
            0.201,
            0.671
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This gives"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.374,
            0.651,
            0.792,
            0.671
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{B} \\equiv \\angle \\mathrm{P} = \\angle \\mathrm{E}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { P Q } \\parallel \\mathrm { E F }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (How?)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.697,
            0.205,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.413,
            0.684,
            0.537,
            0.726
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\left[ \\frac{\\mathrm{DP}}{\\mathrm{PE}} = \\frac{\\mathrm{DQ}}{\\mathrm{QF}} \\right."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.712,
            0.697,
            0.79,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(Why?)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.751,
            0.14,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.736,
            0.79,
            0.78
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "\\left[ \\frac{ AB }{ DE } = \\frac{ AC }{ DF } \\right.\\tag{Why?}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.789,
            0.579,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { \\mathrm { ^ { \\mathrm { \\mathrm { { \\mathrm { { \\mathrm { { \\mathrm { { } } } } } A } } } } B } } } { \\mathrm { { \\mathrm { { \\mathrm { { D E } } } } } } } } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { { \\mathrm { { \\mathrm { { B C } } } } } } } { \\mathrm { { \\mathrm { { E F } } } } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and so "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{AB}}{\\mathrm{DE}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{BC}}{\\mathrm{EF}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{AC}}{\\mathrm{DF}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.84,
            0.902,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Remark :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If two angles of a triangle are respectively equal to two angles of another triangle, then by the angle sum property of a triangle their third angles will also be equal. Therefore, AAA similarity criterion can also be stated as follows:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.966,
            0.563,
            0.983
          ],
